            {
              "key": "post-3",
              "type": "Post",
              "title": "Writing every week, one year later",
              "slug": "writing-every-week",
              "seo_description": "What a year of weekly posts taught me about habits, drafts and hitting publish.",
              "in_menu": true,
              "data": {
                "excerpt": "What a year of weekly posts taught me about habits, drafts and hitting publish.",
                "published": "2026-10-28",
                "author": "Alex Morgan",
                "body": [
                  {
                    "type": "rich_text",
                    "value": {
                      "body": "<p>A year ago I promised myself one post a week. Some weeks it was easy; most weeks it was not.</p><p>The trick turned out to be lowering the bar: a short, honest post beats a perfect one that never ships.</p>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "quote",
                    "value": {
                      "text": "Publishing is a muscle. The more often you use it, the less it hurts.",
                      "attribution": "Alex Morgan"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "rich_text",
                    "value": {
                      "body": "<p>If you are thinking about starting, start small, and start this week.</p>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "cover": "@media:paper"
              }
            },
            {
              "key": "post-2",
              "type": "Post",
              "title": "A calmer way to plan the week",
              "slug": "calmer-week-planning",
              "seo_description": "Three questions on a Sunday evening that make the week ahead feel lighter.",
              "in_menu": true,
              "data": {
                "excerpt": "Three questions on a Sunday evening that make the week ahead feel lighter.",
                "published": "2026-10-14",
                "author": "Alex Morgan",
                "body": [
                  {
                    "type": "rich_text",
                    "value": {
                      "body": "<p>Planning used to mean a long list I never finished. Now it means three questions.</p><p>What must happen? What would make the week good? What can wait? Everything else is noise.</p>"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "quote",
                    "value": {
                      "text": "A plan is a promise to your future self. Keep it small enough to keep.",
                      "attribution": "Alex Morgan"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "rich_text",
                    "value": {
                      "body": "<p>Try it this Sunday and see how Monday feels.</p>"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "cover": "@media:leaves"
              }
            },
            {
